From ba6f18ee8eba196ae3d6057de03e68a8c9dbe20a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dnz3d4c <dnz3d4c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:24:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Compat: point the installer at the Korean profile and a local
 build

The installer is the right shape for this project - Dalamud's own plugin
window is ImGui and a screen reader cannot read it, so the DevPlugin route
is not a workaround, it is the only accessible path. Four things had to
change for the Korean client.

1. Profile root. %APPDATA%\XIVLauncherKR, not XIVLauncher. The Korean
   launcher is a separate program and the two folders coexist.

2. Nothing creates that profile. XIVLauncher builds it on first login on
   the global side; the Korean launcher does not, and the Korean Dalamud
   updater says outright it is not a setup program for a new PC. So the
   installer now builds the three missing pieces itself. The nasty one is
   DALAMUD_RUNTIME: without it the updater still reports success and the
   CLR simply never starts inside the game.

   Where the global build downloads XIVLauncher, this one stops and points
   at the Korean Dalamud updater. We do not redistribute that pipeline.

3. Plugin source is the local build, not a GitHub release. Not for
   convenience: the upstream release binary is bound against
   FFXIVClientStructs 7.55 and Korean Dalamud pins 7.51, so it would load
   and then throw on the first gearset call. It looks beside the EXE first
   (the shipping shape: two files in one folder), then walks up to the
   build output (the developer shape).

4. Korean UI. Loc falls back to English now instead of German - what falls
   through would otherwise be read aloud as a German sentence. The Korean
   dictionary only carries the keys this flow actually shows; translating
   the 130 unused ones would just rot.

Self-update is left in place but not called. There is no release channel
yet, and deleting the machinery makes every rebase on a newer upstream
more expensive - switching it back on is one line in RunAsync.

--check and --bootstrap print what the installer resolves and exit. A
WinForms dialog cannot be inspected without a mouse and a screen, and when
nothing happens the reason is always one of those paths.

FF14ACC_KR_PROFILE overrides the profile root. It covers a moved profile,
and it is how the "nothing exists yet" branch gets exercised on a machine
where everything already exists - that branch is the first one a new user
hits, so it must not be the one nobody has run.

Build: 0 warnings, 0 errors
Verified: --bootstrap on an empty folder creates installedPlugins,
devPlugins and a 72-byte BOM-free dalamudConfig.json, and is idempotent on
a second run. --check resolves all eight paths, and prefers a zip beside
the EXE over the build tree.
